.DS_Store
node_modules/
.build/
tools/SimTapTarget/build/
*.xcodeproj/
DerivedData/
.wrangler/
test-results/
playwright-report/
host/pion-bridge/.svtav1/
tools/WinTapTarget/build/

# The native-receiver checkout + toolchain (12 GB / 776 MB) and its machine-local build
# scratch. Machine-local by nature (a gclient sync + a 30-60 minute ninja build), and
# must live under the repo (see MODULE.bazel's local repositories) without ever being
# committed to it.
third_party/libwebrtc-checkout/
third_party/depot-tools/
third_party/rdev-libwebrtc-build/
third_party/rdev-libwebrtc-install/

# Bazel convenience symlinks (created in the workspace root on every build).
bazel-bin
bazel-out
bazel-rdev
bazel-testlogs

# `go list -m all` from either Go module materialises this at the repo root; the
# commands our scripts actually run (go build/test) do not. Untracked either way.
go.work.sum

# `go build` in host/streaming-engine/PionBridge/ drops its binary here, named after the package.
# It reached a commit once (14 MB, stripped from history before push) because a task staged the
# whole directory. Ignored by FULL PATH rather than by bare name, so an unrelated `pionbridge`
# elsewhere is not silently hidden.
/host/streaming-engine/PionBridge/pionbridge

# Screenshots the browser checks write beside themselves — rail-check and rail-check-desktop drop
# shot-*.png in the repo root, host-sources-probe drops one in e2e/. They are check OUTPUT, not
# evidence: regenerate them by re-running the check. Root-anchored and e2e-anchored so a deliberate
# shot-*.png committed under docs/ (a defect record) is still staged normally.
/shot-*.png
/e2e/shot-*.png

# Agent scratch. Root-anchored, so the COMMITTED design record in docs/superpowers/ is untouched.
# AGENTS.md is the source of truth for every agent; each runtime writes its own scratch directory
# here and a new runtime adds a line to this block rather than a new convention.
/.claude/
/.superpowers/

# Rust build output. The LOCKFILE is committed (host/rdev-noise/Cargo.lock): a crypto dependency
# resolving to a different version between two machines is exactly the drift a lockfile exists to
# stop, and this one sits on the security boundary.
host/rdev-noise/target/

# Bazel names one convenience link after the checkout directory.
/bazel-*
